**Definition 2.2 (captured entries).** The distinguished-entry word of
the chosen archival description is the exact pair

$$
[\mathrm{GCAEntries},\mathrm{ConstructionDirectory}].
$$

GCAEntries includes its SourceEntrySet and SourceExitSet in GCA
Definition 2.3's fixed order. Step and the source locator project this
first component. The second component has CYCLE Definition 2.4's items

$$
[U(\mathrm{callPathIndex}),U(\mathrm{entryPC}),U(\mathrm{exitPC}),
 U(\mathrm{port}),U(\mathrm{family}),U(\mathrm{role})].
$$

Generate it from the final expanded graph after numbering. Include
GCA's mode-block construction sites as ingress roles, its immutable
cover/package sites, and the five stage channels. Multiple exits have
separate items. The parser checks ranges, unique keys, typed roles and
the indicated local opcode variants. Canonical supply uses this exact
generated directory. Role selection projects the second component.
The installation serializer $E$ projects the executable GCA entries and
erases the archival construction directory, as in CYCLE Definition 2.4.
No runtime effect or source permission is encoded by the directory.

The graph contains symbolic edges and fixed entry-slot indices, not
unary literals for its own numbered PCs. Metadata generation consequently
does not change the graph's register count or row count. Captured metadata
digits change capture size, not the already constructed executable graph.

